{"name":"Curd","hex":"#f8e1ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Curd","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Curd"}],"entries":[{"title":"Curd","blocks":[{"text":"Curd is obtained by coagulating milk in a sequential process called curdling. It can be a final dairy product or the first stage in cheesemaking. The coagulation can be caused by adding rennet, a culture, or any edible acidic substance such as lemon juice or vinegar, and then allowing it to coagulate. The increased acidity causes the milk proteins (casein) to tangle into solid masses, or curds. Milk that has been left to sour will also automatically produce curds, and sour milk cheeses are produced this way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Curd_Setting.jpg/330px-Curd_Setting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curd"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg/500px-Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg/500px-Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heating and stirring the curd in the traditional process to make French Beaufort cheese, an Alpine cheese","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFabrication_du_Beaufort_(11).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg/500px-20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg/1280px-20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%